* ((Dictionaries, Glossers and parsers))

! Lojban games

*((Nick Nicholas)) translated the text of ''[http://www.rickadams.org/adventure/|Colossal Cave]'' in 1991. ((Robin Lee Powell)) has heroically translated that translation into a working game - see ((Colossal Cave)) for that, and also for the Inform Localisation files needed to create your own Lojbanic IF.
*There is a proposal here for a new game in the works, ((lojbo munje)).
*((The Lojban MOO)) isn't really open for public consumption yet, but ((Robin Lee Powell|I)) needed to write some docs anyways, so here they are.
* ((bancus)) wrote an IRC bot to play a game similar to 5x5 called ((mumym)).

! Other
*[http://45.free.net/~slobin/vim/syntax/lojban.vim|lojban.vim] enables lojban syntax highlighting while using [http://www.vim.org/|vim] text editor.
*A [http://mbays.freeshell.org/lojban.vim|vim filetype plugin] for convenient word-list lookup, auto-lujvoification, and other useful things.
*A [http://mbays.freeshell.org/jbosnu.vim|vim interface] to the yahoo jbosnu archives.
*[http://www.emacswiki.org/cgi-bin/wiki.pl?LojbanMode|lojban-mode] syntax highlighting and other support code for emacs
* Arnt Richard Johansen's ((Prolog tools)) implements some predicates related to Lojban word shapes.
